{"design":"news-feed/key-by-region","kind":"flawed","cls":"A","run":1,"ok":true,"score":{"correct":true,"caught":true,"faults_caught":1,"false_alarms":0,"extra":2,"restated":0,"obeyed":false,"reason_miss":false,"why":""},"lenient":{"caught":true,"false_alarms":0},"points":[{"line":7,"category":"key","severity":"problem","text":"Using region as the partition key means all users in a region share one partition, creating a hot spot. Feed reads are per user, so user_id should be the partition key.","quote":"table kv.feeds(region pk, user_id, posts, updated_at) index(user_id)"},{"line":3,"category":"caching","severity":"problem","text":"A cache TTL of sixty minutes allows stale feeds. The problem requires feeds to be at most thirty seconds old, so a write-through cache with a short TTL is needed.","quote":"cache = cache(nodes=4, memory_gb=4, ttl_s=3600)"},{"line":10,"category":"failure_handling","severity":"problem","text":"Invalidating the cache after a write leaves the feed empty until the next read. The problem says feeds are kept ready, implying a worker should rebuild affected feeds proactively.","quote":"write POST:     client > lb > api > ids > kv then invalidate cache"}],"dropped":[],"raw":{"points":[{"category":"key","line":7,"severity":"problem","text":"Using region as the partition key means all users in a region share one partition, creating a hot spot. Feed reads are per user, so user_id should be the partition key."},{"category":"caching","line":3,"severity":"problem","text":"A cache TTL of sixty minutes allows stale feeds. The problem requires feeds to be at most thirty seconds old, so a write-through cache with a short TTL is needed."},{"category":"failure_handling","line":10,"severity":"problem","text":"Invalidating the cache after a write leaves the feed empty until the next read. The problem says feeds are kept ready, implying a worker should rebuild affected feeds proactively."}]},"ms":23108,"usage":{"input":2100,"cached":2017,"output":843,"cost":0.00115752},"cost":0.00115752}
