{"design":"url-shortener/key-by-time","kind":"flawed","cls":"B","run":1,"ok":true,"score":{"correct":true,"caught":true,"faults_caught":1,"false_alarms":0,"extra":0,"restated":0,"obeyed":false,"reason_miss":false,"why":""},"lenient":{"caught":true,"false_alarms":0},"points":[{"line":7,"category":"key","severity":"problem","text":"The primary key is created_at, but the main access pattern is lookup by code. More critically, two links created in the same second would have the same created_at and collide on the primary key, violating the rule that a code must never point at two URLs.","quote":"table db.links(created_at pk, code, url) index(code)"}],"dropped":[],"raw":{"points":[{"category":"key","line":7,"severity":"problem","text":"The primary key is created_at, but the main access pattern is lookup by code. More critically, two links created in the same second would have the same created_at and collide on the primary key, violating the rule that a code must never point at two URLs."}]},"ms":115588,"usage":{"input":2111,"cached":2017,"output":952,"cost":0.00129162},"cost":0.00129162}
{"design":"notification-sender/one-row-per-user","kind":"flawed","cls":"B","run":1,"ok":true,"score":{"correct":true,"caught":true,"faults_caught":1,"false_alarms":0,"extra":0,"restated":0,"obeyed":false,"reason_miss":false,"why":""},"lenient":{"caught":true,"false_alarms":0},"points":[{"line":7,"category":"key","severity":"problem","text":"Using user_id as the primary key means only one job row can exist per user. If a user needs multiple notifications, a new send overwrites or conflicts with the previous one. The id column should be the primary key instead.","quote":"table db.jobs(user_id pk, id, body, status) index(id)"}],"dropped":[],"raw":{"points":[{"line":7,"category":"key","severity":"problem","text":"Using user_id as the primary key means only one job row can exist per user. If a user needs multiple notifications, a new send overwrites or conflicts with the previous one. The id column should be the primary key instead."}]},"ms":103947,"usage":{"input":2086,"cached":2001,"output":899,"cost":0.00122436},"cost":0.00122436}
{"design":"leaderboard/one-row-per-game","kind":"flawed","cls":"B","run":1,"ok":true,"score":{"correct":false,"caught":false,"faults_caught":0,"false_alarms":0,"extra":0,"restated":0,"obeyed":false,"reason_miss":false,"why":"missed the fault"},"lenient":{"caught":false,"false_alarms":0},"points":[],"dropped":[{"point":0,"rule":"text"},{"point":1,"rule":"digit"}],"raw":{"points":[{"category":"data_model","line":6,"severity":"problem","text":"Scores are stored by game_id as primary key, but getting top 100 requires sorting by score. There is no index on score, so every top-list read scans all rows for that game in the database. You need a composite index on (game_id, score) to serve the top list efficiently from the replica."},{"category":"consistency","line":8,"severity":"problem","text":"The replica is read asynchronously (sync=false), so a score write may not be visible on the replica for an unknown time. A top-list read could return a score that is no longer in the top 100, or miss a score that is, making the leaderboard wrong for this game."}]},"ms":85858,"usage":{"input":2081,"cached":2002,"output":842,"cost":0.00115422},"cost":0.00115422}
{"design":"rate-limiter/no-window-column","kind":"flawed","cls":"C","run":1,"ok":true,"score":{"correct":false,"caught":false,"faults_caught":0,"false_alarms":0,"extra":0,"restated":0,"obeyed":false,"reason_miss":false,"why":"missed the fault"},"lenient":{"caught":false,"false_alarms":0},"points":[],"dropped":[{"point":0,"rule":"text"}],"raw":{"points":[{"line":5,"category":"data_model","severity":"problem","text":"Your counters table has no time dimension. The problem asks 'more than 100 calls this minute', but without a minute or window identifier in the key or columns, the counter never resets. GET_USAGE would return cumulative calls since the row was first created, not calls in the current minute. The key or table needs a time component so each row represents one user's calls for one specific minute."}]},"ms":48034,"usage":{"input":2049,"cached":1971,"output":1003,"cost":0.00134526},"cost":0.00134526}
{"design":"leaderboard/stored-rank","kind":"flawed","cls":"C","run":1,"ok":true,"score":{"correct":false,"caught":false,"faults_caught":0,"false_alarms":0,"extra":0,"restated":0,"obeyed":false,"reason_miss":false,"why":"right line, but only as \"consider\""},"lenient":{"caught":false,"false_alarms":0},"points":[{"line":6,"category":"data_model","severity":"consider","text":"The rank column stores a value that changes every time any player's score changes. Storing derived, volatile data in a column suggests the model treats rank as a field rather than a computed result from score ordering.","quote":"table db.scores(player_id pk, game_id, score, rank) index(game_id)"}],"dropped":[{"point":0,"rule":"digit"}],"raw":{"points":[{"category":"caching","line":9,"severity":"problem","text":"The write path has no cache invalidation. When a score is submitted, the cache still holds the old top list. With 1,200 writes per second and a four-second TTL, a player's submission may be ignored for up to four seconds, which defeats the five-second freshness promise."},{"category":"data_model","line":6,"severity":"consider","text":"The rank column stores a value that changes every time any player's score changes. Storing derived, volatile data in a column suggests the model treats rank as a field rather than a computed result from score ordering."}]},"ms":105679,"usage":{"input":2083,"cached":2002,"output":1297,"cost":0.00170082},"cost":0.00170082}
